# Ghostty configuration.
#
# Lives at the XDG path rather than
# ~/Library/Application Support/com.mitchellh.ghostty/config.ghostty because
# Ghostty reads both on macOS and only this one on Linux. Note it MERGES the
# two when both exist, so keep only this one.
#
# TERMINAL APPEARANCE ONLY. The shell itself — prompt, history, aliases,
# completion, secrets — is global: every terminal and SSH session reads
# ~/.zshrc and ~/.zprofile. Nothing shell-related is set here, so there is
# exactly one obvious place to change the shell: the dotfiles repo's dot_zshrc.

# The theme follows the OS appearance: Ghostty auto-switches between the two
# (light:<name>,dark:<name>). Deliberately asymmetric: dark is Gruvbox
# *Material* Dark, light is plain Gruvbox Light *Hard* -- preference. The
# rest of the stack follows the same signal: the zsh prompt uses indexed
# colors 0-15, Neovim sets 'background' from the OS
# (lua/bruce/core/appearance.lua), and delta-theme (~/.local/bin, wired into
# git and lazygit) picks the matching delta syntax theme.
{{- /*
  The two names above come from .chezmoidata/palette.toml ([palette.scheme])
  -- the single source of truth for colors. A scheme change is an edit there
  plus `chezmoi apply`, never here.
*/}}
theme = light:{{ .palette.scheme.light_theme }},dark:{{ .palette.scheme.dark_theme }}
